{"summary":"Restore payload visibility for Status stringification modes.","explanation":"The failures share one mode-handling cause across the public API and heap-backed renderer. With a status containing payloads `foo=bar` and `bar=\xff`, `Status.ToString()` and the default-based ostream and `absl::StrCat(status)` paths produce only `INTERNAL: fail`, so the assertions expecting `[foo='bar']` and `[bar='\\xff']` fail. `Status.ToString(mode)` currently discards `mode` and always passes `kWithEverything`; then `StatusRep::ToString` checks whether the mode equals `kWithPayload`, so `kWithEverything` does not print payloads. Forward the caller’s mode and test the payload bit. This keeps `kWithNoExtraData` and `~kWithPayload` payload-free while enabling payloads for `kWithPayload` and `kWithEverything`.","edits":[{"path":"absl/status/status.h","old":"inline std::string Status::ToString(StatusToStringMode mode) const {
  return ok() ? "OK" : ToStringSlow(rep_, StatusToStringMode::kWithEverything);
}","new":"inline std::string Status::ToString(StatusToStringMode mode) const {
  return ok() ? "OK" : ToStringSlow(rep_, mode);
}"},{"path":"absl/status/internal/status_internal.cc","old":"  const bool with_payload = mode == StatusToStringMode::kWithPayload;","new":"  const bool with_payload =
      (mode & StatusToStringMode::kWithPayload) == StatusToStringMode::kWithPayload;"}]}
